Context: read only what's needed, start with nearby files. Consult ARCHITECTURE.md or README.md only when the task scope requires it — don't re-read files already in context.

Code: minimal diffs, match existing style/patterns, reuse before creating, no unnecessary abstractions or refactors.

Output: concise, actionable, note tradeoffs briefly.